# SmartiQo Project AI Rules

You are working in a STATIC CLONE of a Next.js Single Page Application (SPA).
Because this is a static export, YOU CANNOT AND MUST NOT EDIT HTML FILES directly (`index.html` or `pages/*.html`). If you do, React Hydration will immediately overwrite your changes when the page loads in the browser.

## CRITICAL RULES FOR UI/LOGIC UPDATES:

1. **NEVER EDIT HTML FILES DIRECTLY.** Do not modify `index.html` or files in the `pages/` directory to make UI or text changes.
2. **ALL CHANGES MUST GO IN `my-custom-changes.js`**. 
3. **USE SmartiqoInjector**. To modify the DOM, you must use the custom `SmartiqoInjector` framework which waits for React Hydration to finish before applying changes.

### How to use SmartiqoInjector (in `my-custom-changes.js`):

**For DOM Changes / Text Updates / Event Listeners:**
```javascript
SmartiqoInjector.watch('your-css-selector', (element) => {
    // This callback runs AFTER React hydration has rendered the element
    element.textContent = 'New Text';
    
    element.addEventListener('click', () => {
        // custom logic
    });
});
```

**For CSS Styling Updates:**
```javascript
SmartiqoInjector.injectCSS(`
    .your-custom-class {
        background-color: #ff0000 !important;
    }
`);
```

**For modifying inline styles of specific Next.js components:**
Always rely on `SmartiqoInjector.watch()` targeting specific classes, tags, or IDs. 

DO NOT attempt to look for standard React `.jsx` or `.tsx` files. They do not exist in this workspace. Everything is pre-bundled in `_next/static/`.

Follow these rules perfectly and your UI updates will succeed.
